#### 8. Exception Handling — `addNullSkuManualCatch`
**Lines 92–99.** Manual `try/catch` + `fail()` instead of JUnit 5's `assertThrows`. The `catch (Exception ex)` is also overly broad — it would catch any exception type, not just the expected one.

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

**Fix:** Use `assertThrows`:

```java
@Test void addThrowsOnNullSku() {
    var ex = assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("sku is required"));
}
```

